menu "CEC comms (CAN/TWAI)"

    config CEC_CAN_BITRATE_BPS
        int "CAN bus bitrate (bps)"
        default 125000
        help
            PRODUCTION TARGET IS 500000 (matches the 24-pin + Hub
            platform spec, classical CAN at 500 kbps). The default is
            parked at the bench rate of 125000 because the Waveshare
            SN65HVD230 bench breakout ties the transceiver Rs pin to
            GND through a 10 kohm resistor, putting it in slope-control
            mode; the slewed edges trip the controller's bit-monitoring
            at 500 kbps and the node bus-offs every few seconds, while
            125 kbps gives the edges enough margin.

            Raise to 500000 once either the bench breakout's Rs pin is
            bridged directly to GND (forcing high-speed mode), or the
            firmware runs against the production CAN front-end where Rs
            is wired straight to GND by design.

    config CEC_CAN_DIAG_LISTEN_ONLY
        bool "Force listen-only mode (bus-off triage diagnostic)"
        default n
        help
            Forces the controller into listen-only mode (no TX, no ACK,
            just RX-monitor). If bus-off still happens with this on,
            the controller / wire / bias is fundamentally broken and
            the TX path isn't the cause. If bus-off stops with this on
            but resumes with it off, every TX attempt is the trigger
            and the issue is downstream of TXD. Leave off for normal
            operation.

    config CEC_CAN_TX_GPIO
        int "CAN TX GPIO"
        default 4
        help
            TWAI TX pin (board wiring; the eps daughterboard uses 4).

    config CEC_CAN_RX_GPIO
        int "CAN RX GPIO"
        default 15
        help
            TWAI RX pin (board wiring; the eps daughterboard uses 15).

endmenu
